    "b-ks2-path-event-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-event-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "REGRESSION — The event pathway ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "index_task.pathway",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). Fires when a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " event row lands on a target's ledger: the run-loop inserts it at an integration failure or an epoch boundary when a merge conflicts away a previously good result; report reconciliation inserts the upstream variant, with a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "commit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ref, when an upstream change breaks a formerly matched target. Facts are never auto-invalidated — a broken score is not a changed claim. The librarian re-examines the affected target's live facts and revises only where the claim about meaning changed, citing the records behind the event's refs; the event row itself is never citable."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
