    },
    "b-ks2-path-event-librarian-reads": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-event-librarian-reads",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The librarian reads the event and its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event_ref",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows through the derived ledger view, then the records the refs name — the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows behind a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ref, the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pull_request",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row behind a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ref — alongside the live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows for the event's target, the one subject affected. Search: the structured attempts query pulls the referenced run and its score trajectory, keyword over its transcript where the why matters, and the code graph shows what the boundary merge or upstream commit left in the checkout."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-event-librarian-writes": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-event-librarian-writes",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The facts do not change because the score did. Where the break changed what we believe — a match that turned out to hang on a fragile idiom, a claim the conflicting merge disproved — the librarian overwrites the fact in place or clears it; where the claim stands, it re-cites. Every citation is an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locator into the records the event's refs name — events themselves are not a knowledge source, have no locator grammar, and never appear in an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row. The event row stays as it is: append-only ledger, addressed to the next worker, not to the graph."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-event-coverage-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-event-coverage-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Coverage"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-event-coverage-p": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-event-coverage-p",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "No watermark moves: events are ledger rows, not a watermarked source, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "source_watermark",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " has no row for them. The inserting agent writes one "
        },
        {
          "insert": "index_task",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pathway",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "payload",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " naming the affected target; the librarian claims and completes it by timestamps and stamps the target's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "subject_index_state",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row at pass completion. A regression whose task has no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "done_at",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " has not been looked at — the worker sees it in the ledger either way; the queue only tracks the librarian's pass."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
